Description: Keep output mirroring consistent for output management clients
 Display configuration tools (wdisplays, kanshi, regolith-displayd) use
 the wlr-output-management protocol, where a mirror is reported as an
 enabled head at its source's position. With 14-output-mirroring.patch
 alone, a configuration that placed the mirror elsewhere was silently
 ignored while mirroring continued, a configuration that only changed the
 mirror's scale or transform stored the source's position as the
 mirror's own (so after `mirror off` it sat on top of its source), and
 `output ... mirror` could change what the reported heads mean without a
 new configuration serial.
 .
 Each output management configuration now decides every mirror again, on
 the layout the whole configuration leads to: a mirror head enabled away
 from its source's resulting position suspends mirroring, and the output
 works as a normal output there while keeping its mirror setting; a
 mirror head left out or placed at its source mirrors. Applying the
 reported heads unchanged keeps mirroring. The suspension lasts through
 other outputs' hotplugs and ends with the next output management
 configuration, an output command for the mirror, a config reload, or
 the source being disconnected. Tests decide the same way and change
 nothing. The position sent for a mirror that keeps mirroring isn't
 stored, and output commands or reloads that may change mirroring send a
 new configuration serial.
